## Ironclad engineering standards

### Language

All project content and output — code, comments, commit messages,
identifiers, documentation, and chat responses when producing project
artifacts — is written in English, regardless of what language the user
writes their prompts in.

### AI usage policy (condensed)

- This assistant supports engineering decisions, it does not replace
  engineering ownership. The developer who accepts, modifies, merges, or
  deploys code remains responsible for it. AI-generated code gets the
  same review, tests, and standards as any other code.
- Never paste real student or guardian personal data into a session to
  debug an issue; use synthetic or anonymized data instead.
- Confirmation protocol: a short plan and explicit go-ahead before coding
  for schema changes, new dependencies, architectural decisions,
  significant restructuring, major version upgrades, or genuinely
  ambiguous requirements. Not required for clear bug fixes, missing
  tests, small isolated functions, or formatting.
- State low-stakes assumptions in one line instead of silently picking
  one or stopping to ask.
- If the same approach fails twice in a row, stop and report instead of
  trying further variations unprompted.
- Touch only what the task requires; flag unrelated cleanup as a
  suggestion instead of doing it inline.
- Prefer the most recent stable or long-term-support version of a
  language, runtime, or framework that still receives security patches.
  Dependencies stay pinned in a lockfile.

### Task routing

Read `{{CONTENT_DIR}}/ai-usage-policy.md` and
`{{CONTENT_DIR}}/language.md` regardless of task type. Then, per task:

| Task type | Read |
|---|---|
| API or backend implementation | {{CONTENT_DIR}}/architecture.md, {{CONTENT_DIR}}/backend.md |
| Database or query work | {{CONTENT_DIR}}/architecture.md, {{CONTENT_DIR}}/database.md |
| Authentication or security-sensitive work | {{CONTENT_DIR}}/architecture.md, {{CONTENT_DIR}}/security.md |
| Writing or fixing tests | {{CONTENT_DIR}}/architecture.md, {{CONTENT_DIR}}/testing.md |
| Debugging an issue or a production incident | {{CONTENT_DIR}}/debug.md, {{CONTENT_DIR}}/testing.md |
| Refactoring existing code | {{CONTENT_DIR}}/refactor.md, {{CONTENT_DIR}}/testing.md, {{CONTENT_DIR}}/architecture.md |
| Writing a commit message | {{CONTENT_DIR}}/commits.md |
| Logging or monitoring | {{CONTENT_DIR}}/observability.md |
| External integration (email, SMS, calendar, or similar) | {{CONTENT_DIR}}/backend.md, {{CONTENT_DIR}}/resilience.md |
| Anything touching student or guardian data | {{CONTENT_DIR}}/lgpd.md, {{CONTENT_DIR}}/security.md |
| Code review | {{CONTENT_DIR}}/review-checklist.md |

